    {
      "v": 3,
      "zh": "当时河西的总督达乃和示他・波斯乃，并他们的同党来问说：「谁降旨让你们建造这殿，修成这墙呢？」",
      "en": "At that time Tattenai governor of Trans-Euphrates, Shethar-Bozenai, and their colleagues came to them and asked, “Who gave you authority[NOTE:1] to rebuild this temple and to complete this structure?”[NOTE:2]",
      "notes": [
        "Aram “who placed to you a command?” So also v. 9.",
        "The exact meaning of the Aramaic word אֻשַּׁרְנָא (ʾussarnaʾ) here and in v. 9 is uncertain (BDB 1083 s.v.). The LXX and Vulgate understand it to mean “wall.” Here it is used in collocation with בַּיְתָא (baytaʾ, “house” as the temple of God), while in 5:3, 9 it is used in parallelism with this term. It might be related to the Assyrian noun ashurru (“wall”) or ashru (“sanctuary”; so BDB). F. Rosenthal, who translates the word “furnishings,” thinks that it probably enters Aramaic from Persian (Grammar, 62-63, §189)."
      ],
